SOUND EFFECTS: synthesized in code by ../kit/tools/mix.py with the library's core/audio/sfx.py (whooshes on three cuts and on the
  band, a swish on the push-in, a pop on the 14775 plate, a low impact on the logo, a thud on the sign-off card). No recordings
  or samples. No narration.

STYLE AND CODE: the look, the plate material and the story are taken from a HyperFrames trailer of the game made by the library's
  author (its SPEC, its three story options and its v002 cut); the film here is rebuilt on the library's page contract with
  ../kit/: no HyperFrames, no GSAP, no <video> playback (the clips are cut into frames on the film's frame grid by
  ../kit/tools/clips.py). ../kit/page/tween.js comes from Tech Launch's tween.js (same library), with clip-path added;
  ../kit/tools/beats.py is adapted from Scrapbook Song's analyze.py (same library).

TOOLS: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame capture,
  events export, reading-time check, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; neo/audio/cues.py, neo/audio/master.py,
  neo/render/remote.sh.

ON SCREEN: the game's own end (the logo on the iron band, Demo 试玩已上线, TapTap 搜索「归路：新旅途」, PC · 安卓 · iOS) is part of
